Make Vercel build robust + stop per-push security audit emails

Vercel
- New scripts/vercel-build.sh: defensive build that detects whether
  Vercel runs us from the repo root (and we must `cd easy-locs-ea1eb0ed`)
  or directly from inside the inner project, runs install + build in the
  right cwd, then symlinks dist/ to the start dir so the output is
  visible regardless of Vercel's 'Root Directory' setting.
- vercel.json now calls the script and uses outputDirectory: 'dist',
  which resolves correctly in both layouts (the symlink covers the case
  where Root Directory is the repo root).
- Replaces the previous `cd easy-locs-ea1eb0ed && npm install && npm run build`
  inline command, which broke as soon as the project's Root Directory
  was nudged off the repo root.
- Self-tested locally: simulated repo-root cwd, build artifact lands at
  both ./easy-locs-ea1eb0ed/dist and (via symlink) ./dist.

Security Audit workflow
- Removed the `push: branches: [main]` trigger. The four jobs
  (npm audit gate, Semgrep SAST, Orbit E2EE crypto tests, edge-fn
  inventory drift) were already failing on main BEFORE these
  closeouts and were emailing the maintainer on every commit.
- Pull-request runs still gate merges; the weekly cron + manual
  workflow_dispatch keep the audit safety net in place.
- Re-enabling `push` belongs to sibling LB task #846 (the actual
  fix-the-failing-jobs work).
